Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: add opt-in per-MAC roaming path diagnostics

For mt79xx 7.6.7.3 after the Build17 42-patch series. Default off.
No forwarding, station lifetime, isolation or acceleration policy changes.
Capture packet metadata before forwarding, mark actual decision branches,
and capture the WCID/wdev actually written to the forwarding descriptor.
Packet logs do not re-read entry/wdev/skb after submission. Slot observations
and deletion counters are not an atomic station-generation guarantee.
send_data_pkt return codes prove submission only, not RF delivery.
Log originating maintenance decisions and peer management reason codes.
Shared budgets of 64 packet-stage and 16 deletion/management log records
per HZ window expose suppression through read-only roam_diag_stats.
Counters are cumulative and not a cross-counter snapshot. Missing output
alone never proves path absence.
Packet scope: selected MACs, untagged IPv4 TCP SYN/RST, selected port.
Management/deletion scope: selected MACs, metadata and reason codes only.

